    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d8">

                <pb facs="0015" n="6" xml:id="pg6"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.H/48: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-03-18T15:00:00-03:00">March 18, 1938—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 18—1:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>59. For the Under Secretary. Your telegram 36, March 14, 3 p.m. Aranha<anchor
                        n="8" xml:id="d8-f1"/> told me today that he agreed entirely with your
                    attitude about the Lima Conference.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d8-f1" n="8" xml:id="d8-f1-content">
                <p>Oswaldo Aranha, Brazilian Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
